<title>UNITED NATIONS: U.N. SAYS IRAQI OIL CONTRACT APPROVALS RISE TO 12.</title>
<headline>U.N. SAYS IRAQI OIL CONTRACT APPROVALS RISE TO 12.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved 12 Iraqi oil contracts for the second round of the &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal through August 12, according to U.N. officials on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Total barrels for the dozen approvals is 69.22 million barrels, and includes deals with companies from eight nations. U.N. information does not detail each oil company, but instead lists the country of origin for each contract.</p>
<p>The U.N. also does not give the length of the term contracts, and whether the deals apply to only the first period of the 180-day accord.</p>
<p>Following is an updated list of the contract volumes and nationality of the receiving company:</p>
<p>Contract No. 1 - 5.5 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Contract No. 2 - 6.12 million barrels/French</p>
<p>Contract No. 3 - 2.7 million barrels/Italian</p>
<p>Contract No. 4 - 13.5 million barrels/Turkish</p>
<p>Contract No. 5 - 3.6 million barrels/Swiss</p>
<p>Contract No. 6 - 3.6 million barrels/U.S.</p>
<p>Contract No. 7 - 1.8 million barrels/Turkish</p>
<p>Contract No. 8 - 5.4 million barrels/Spanish</p>
<p>Contract No. 9 - 5.4 million barrels/French</p>
<p>Contract No. 10 - 7.2 million barrels/Russian</p>
<p>Contract No. 11 - 3.6 million barrels/U.S.</p>
<p>Contract No. 12 - 10.8 million barrels/Dutch</p>
<p>Iraq is allowed to sell $2.14 billion worth of crude from June 8 to December 6. The deal requires Iraq to export up to $1 billion in two separate 90-day periods, the first one ending on September 5.</p>
<p>((Patrick Connole, United Nations, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
